    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nnew\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski, would you be open to introducing a mini.bookmarks module? \n\nI'm making use of [my own version](https://github.com/justEstif/dotfiles/blob/main/nvim/.config/nvim/plugin/09-marks.lua) built upon a [this reddit post](https://www.reddit.com/r/neovim/comments/1gz1964/global_marks_specific_to_a_project/).\n\nHowever, I think it would fit in well with the mini.nvim module.\n\nAnd now the ✨pitch✨\n\n---\n\nA Git and context-aware bookmarks module with the core features being:\n\n- Context-sensitive bookmark persistence (per Git repo/branch/directory) via Mini.git integration\n- Fuzzy bookmark search via Mini.picks integration\n- Tagging with Mini.visits\n- Automatic bookmarks at code landmarks using Mini.hipatterns\n- Visual gutter indicators matching Mini.map conventions\n- Smart bookmark maintenance (auto-removal of invalid marks)\n",
