        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Sorry, I don't think it is a good fit for 'mini.visits'. It was considered, but it would require substantial redesign of 'mini.visits' as a whole. Currently labels functionality is a relatively small build on top of existing path visit autotracking: it adds a `labels` field to the index entry which doesn't have to be verified in the future. Adding position would also mean extra work for keeping its track and validity. Besides, I am not entirely sure that persistent position-aware labels doesn't get outdated very quickly: files can have text changed and positions will point to something else.\n\nI am grateful for the enthusiasm, but I think I am going to close this as unplanned.",
